From: challoc <noreply@chainguard.dev>
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Pass the allocation start to zmalloc_size for kvobj in
 DEBUG SDSLEN and MEMORY USAGE

A kvobj with metadata (an expire) has its metadata in front of the
object, so the kvobj pointer is not the start of its allocation:
kvobjGetAllocPtr() is, as decrRefCount() and the defrag code already use.
DEBUG SDSLEN (debug.c) and MEMORY USAGE of a module key
(kvobjComputeSize, object.c) asked zmalloc_usable_size()/zmalloc_size()
for the kvobj pointer itself.

The bundled jemalloc looks sizes up by address and answers for an
interior pointer too, so the results there are unchanged. An allocator
that checks the pointer it is given (challoc aborts on a pointer that is
not a block start; libc's malloc_usable_size reads the header in front of
it and returns garbage) does not: under challoc the unit/type/string test
"Check MEMORY USAGE for embedded key strings with jemalloc" crashed the
server. Independent of the allocator patches; still present on Redis's
unstable branch.
---
 src/debug.c  | 4 +++-
 src/object.c | 4 +++-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/debug.c b/src/debug.c
--- a/src/debug.c
+++ b/src/debug.c
@@ -759,7 +759,9 @@ NULL
         } else {
             /* The key's allocation size reflects the entire robj allocation.  
              * For embedded values, report an allocation size of 0. */
-            size_t obj_alloc = zmalloc_usable_size(val);
+            /* With metadata (an expire) in front of the object, val is not
+             * the start of its allocation: ask for the block kvobj lives in. */
+            size_t obj_alloc = zmalloc_usable_size(kvobjGetAllocPtr(val));
             size_t val_alloc = val->encoding == OBJ_ENCODING_RAW ? sdsAllocSize(val->ptr) : 0;
             addReplyStatusFormat(c,
                 "key_sds_len:%lld, key_sds_avail:%lld, key_zmalloc: %lld, "
diff --git a/src/object.c b/src/object.c
--- a/src/object.c
+++ b/src/object.c
@@ -1339,7 +1339,9 @@ size_t kvobjComputeSize(robj *key, kvobj *o, size_t sample_size, int dbid) {
     {
         return kvobjAllocSize(o);
     } else if (o->type == OBJ_MODULE) {
-        return zmalloc_size(o) + moduleGetMemUsage(key, o, sample_size, dbid);
+        /* The allocation starts at kvobjGetAllocPtr(o) when metadata (an
+         * expire) precedes the object. */
+        return zmalloc_size(kvobjGetAllocPtr(o)) + moduleGetMemUsage(key, o, sample_size, dbid);
     }
     serverPanic("Unknown object type");
 }
